<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How Sourcedreviews uses affiliate links and how that affects our recommendations."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <header>
      <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
      <p class="summary">How affiliate links work on Sourcedreviews and what they mean for you.</p>
    </header>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>Some links on Sourcedreviews are affiliate links. When you click one and buy something, we may receive a commission from the brand or affiliate network. The price you pay is not affected.</p>

    <h2>The longer version</h2>
    <p>Sourcedreviews participates in affiliate programs with various brands and affiliate networks. Some links in our articles route through those networks using parameters that let the program attribute any resulting purchase to Sourcedreviews. If a purchase is attributed, we may earn a commission.</p>
    <p>Affiliate relationships do not influence which products we recommend. Our editorial process is described on <a href="/our-method/">Our Method</a>; our independence is described on <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Where affiliate links appear</h2>
    <p>Affiliate links appear in product roundups and individual reviews. They are not always visually distinguishable from regular links. The existence of the affiliate relationship is disclosed here and on every article that contains them.</p>

    <h2>FTC compliance</h2>
    <p>This disclosure is provided in accordance with the U.S. Federal Trade Commission's Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and Testimonials in Advertising (16 C.F.R. Part 255).</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>If you have questions about our affiliate relationships, write to <a href="mailto:contact@sourcedreviews.com">contact@sourcedreviews.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>